itional))));\n}\n\n/// A fitting sequential pass charges its peak, not the sum of the module\n/// forecasts it recorded, so later live attribution must report that peak.\npub(super) fn complete_sequential_precharge(forecast: usize) {\n    PRECHARGE_BYTES.with(|bytes| bytes.set(forecast));\n}\n\n/// Name the bound that refused and the module that drove it. The message\n/// itself stays byte-identical, because nested workspace routes remap a\n/// `builder_bytes` refusal by comparing it exactly.\nfn builder_bytes_help(maximum: usize) -> String {\n    crate::bounded_output::budgeted_format(format_args!(\"{}\", BorrowedBuilderHelp(maximum)))\n}\n/// Borrow report content only; this is never a budget or publication owner.\npub(super) struct BorrowedBuilderHelp(pub(super) usize);\nimpl std::fmt::Display for BorrowedBuilderHelp {\n    fn fmt(&self, f: &mut std::fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> std::fmt::Result {\n        write_builder_bytes_help(self.0, f)\n    }\n}\nfn write_builder_bytes_help(maximum: usize, output: &mut dyn std::fmt::Write) -> std::fmt::Result {\n    let precharge = BUILDER_PHASE.with(Cell::get) == BuilderPhase::Precharge;\n    let modules = PRECHARGE_MODULES.with(Cell::get);\n    let forecast = PRECHARGE_BYTES.with(Cell::get);\n    PRECHARGE_DOMINANT.with(|dominant| {\n        let dominant = dominant.borrow();\n        PRECHARGE_PENDING.with(|pending| {\n            let pending = pending.borrow();\n    if let (true, Some(path)) = (precharge, pending.as_ref()) {\n        return write!(output,\n            \"the static admission pre-charge refused before the graph builder ran, while forecasting module `{path}` on its own: that one module does not fit the {maximum}-byte budget, which already carries {forecast} bytes for {modules} earlier module(s). Splitting `{path}` into several modules cannot reduce the forecast, because the pre-charge sums every reachable module; reducing its admitted source can.\"\n        );\n    }\n    if precharge {\n        if let Some((modules,retained,additional)) = PRECHARGE_LATER.with(Cell::get) {\n            return write!(output,\n                \"the static admission pre-charge refused before the graph builder ran, in its final retained-validation forecast: all {modules} module(s) retain {retained} bytes of filtered output, and one function's maximum rebuild scratch plus the canonical lookup directory requires {additional} more bytes beside that complete retained output, which exceeds the {maximum}-byte budget. Resolver and fixed-function allowances remain complete; no individual module owns this later cross-module window.\"\n            );\n        }","before":"}\n\n/// One refused step of the final uncached forecast. That forecast is a\n/// sequential peak over retained filtered output, not a sum of complete module\n/// forecasts, so a summed attribution cannot describe it.\n#[derive(Clone)]\nstruct SequentialRefusal {\n    path: String,\n    earlier: usize,\n    retained: usize,\n    additional: usize,\n    resolving: bool,\n}\n\n/// Restores the previous phase on drop, so a pre-charge nested inside another\n/// one cannot leave live accumulation mislabelled.\npub(super) struct PrechargeScope(BuilderPhase);\n\nimpl Drop for PrechargeScope {\n    fn drop(&mut self) {\n        BUILDER_PHASE.with(|phase| phase.set(self.0));\n    }\n}\n\npub(super) fn precharge_scope() -> PrechargeScope {\n    PrechargeScope(BUILDER_PHASE.with(|phase| phase.replace(BuilderPhase::Precharge)))\n}\n\n/// Start one forecast pass. Every fallback receipt re-costs each module, so\n/// attribution keeps only the pass that is currently running.\npub(super) fn begin_precharge_pass() {\n    PRECHARGE_MODULES.with(|modules| modules.set(0));\n    PRECHARGE_BYTES.with(|bytes| bytes.set(0));\n    PRECHARGE_DOMINANT.with(|dominant| *dominant.borrow_mut() = None);\n    PRECHARGE_PENDING.with(|pending| *pending.borrow_mut() = None);\n    PRECHARGE_SEQUENTIAL.with(|sequential| *sequential.borrow_mut() = None);\n}\n\n/// Name the m